<main id="main">

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow hero-eyebrow">Independent Research — Macro / Equity / Portfolio Strategy</p>
      <h1>Kevin Kamberi</h1>
      <p class="role">Investment Research · Macroeconomics · Portfolio Strategy — Eindhoven, NL</p>

      <p class="lede hero-lede">Independent research on financial markets, macroeconomics, investment themes and portfolio strategy.</p>

      <div class="metric-strip">
        <div class="metric-item"><div class="n">€200K</div><div class="l">AUM</div></div>
        <div class="metric-item"><div class="n">13.8%</div><div class="l">Expected Return</div></div>
        <div class="metric-item"><div class="n">20.1%</div><div class="l">Volatility</div></div>
        <div class="metric-item"><div class="n">0.59</div><div class="l">Sharpe Ratio</div></div>
        <div class="metric-item"><div class="n">0.73</div><div class="l">Portfolio Correlation</div></div>
        <div class="metric-item"><div class="n">9</div><div class="l">Published Notes</div></div>
        <div class="metric-item"><div class="n">5</div><div class="l">Investment Themes</div></div>
        <div class="metric-item"><div class="n">3&nbsp;yrs</div><div class="l">Following Markets</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bordered">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2>Latest research</h2>
        <a class="text-link" href="research.html">View all publications →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="grid reveal">
        <a class="card cat-portfolio" href="research/all-weather-sleeves.html">
          <div class="card-top">
            <span class="card-tag">Markets &amp; Portfolio Strategy</span>
            <span class="card-num">WP 25-01</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Constructing All-Weather Sleeves in a Higher-for-Longer Regime</h3>
          <p class="abstract">An updated framework for diversified sleeves adapted to a structurally higher rate regime, beyond the traditional stock-bond-commodity split.</p>
          <div class="card-foot"><span>21 Jan 2025</span><span>11 pages</span></div>
        </a>

        <a class="card cat-macro" href="research/sticky-services-inflation.html">
          <div class="card-top">
            <span class="card-tag">Macroeconomics</span>
            <span class="card-num">WP 24-04</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Disinflation's Second Mile: Structural Drivers of Sticky Services Inflation</h3>
          <p class="abstract">Why services inflation has proven more persistent than goods, and what that implies for how long policy should stay restrictive.</p>
          <div class="card-foot"><span>02 Aug 2024</span><span>8 pages</span></div>
        </a>

        <a class="card cat-invest" href="research/foundry-capital-intensity.html">
          <div class="card-top">
            <span class="card-tag">Investment &amp; Sector Research</span>
            <span class="card-num">WP 24-02</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Semiconductor Capital Intensity and the Reshaping of Foundry Economics</h3>
          <p class="abstract">Rising capital intensity at the leading edge is concentrating foundry economics — and pricing power — among a narrower set of manufacturers.</p>
          <div class="card-foot"><span>27 Apr 2024</span><span>9 pages</span></div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt bordered">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2>Coverage</h2>
        <p style="max-width:34ch; font-size:14.5px; color:var(--muted); margin:0;">Three lenses on the same question: where is the cycle, what does it mean for fundamentals, and how should a portfolio be built around it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="tiles reveal">
        <a class="tile" href="research.html?cat=macro" onclick="sessionStorage.setItem('kk-filter','macro')">
          <span class="tile-bar"></span>
          <span class="n">01 — Top down</span>
          <h3>Macroeconomics</h3>
          <p>Central bank policy, liquidity, inflation dynamics and the business cycle — the backdrop every allocation decision sits inside.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="tile" href="research.html?cat=invest" onclick="sessionStorage.setItem('kk-filter','invest')">
          <span class="tile-bar"></span>
          <span class="n">02 — Bottom up</span>
          <h3>Investment &amp; Sector Research</h3>
          <p>Sector cycles, capital allocation and competitive structure — where the macro view meets company and industry fundamentals.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="tile" href="research.html?cat=portfolio" onclick="sessionStorage.setItem('kk-filter','portfolio')">
          <span class="tile-bar"></span>
          <span class="n">03 — Construction</span>
          <h3>Markets &amp; Portfolio Strategy</h3>
          <p>Translating a macro and sector view into position sizing, hedging and portfolio construction across regimes.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="two-col reveal">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:16px;">Approach</p>
          <p class="lede">Most research shows a conclusion. I try to show the reasoning — the data, the counter-arguments considered, and the conditions under which the view would be wrong.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>Each note follows the same structure: an abstract stating the claim plainly, key findings that can be checked against data, and a discussion section that engages with the strongest objections. Publication dates and working paper numbers are kept so views can be tracked — and revised in public — over time.</p>
          <p><a class="text-link" href="about.html">More about my background →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

